#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:527
msgid ""
"The zoom the app starts at, and Ctrl+0 returns to. Ctrl with + or -, or the "
"mouse wheel, still zooms for the session."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:528
msgid ""
"Each theme is four colors: background, text, accent and highlight. Every "
"other color of the app is worked out from them, except those of the "
"connection profiles."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:529
msgid ""
"The colors of JSON, YAML, XML and Redisql text. One that would be hard to "
"read on the theme's background is brought closer to its text color."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:530
msgid ""
"How many entries of each key (hash fields, list items, set members...) the "
"global search reads. Fewer is faster, but a match deeper inside a big key is "
"missed."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:531
msgid ""
"The view a key shows when its tab opens. A query's result always opens as a "
"table, and a search hit or a link to a field in the fields view."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:532
msgid ""
"Cachemire reconnects to the connection it was closed on, with its tabs and "
"open folders. An AWS connection signs in again first, in the browser if its "
"session has expired."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:533
msgid ""
"Each time Cachemire starts, it looks for a newer version on the channel "
"picked in About (the i button of the title bar), and opens it when there is "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:534
msgid ""
"The global search lets Redis filter the data itself, so far less of it "
"travels. It uses the server's CPU while it runs, needs permission to run "
"scripts, and goes back to the normal search if the server refuses."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:535
msgid ""
"The active profile logs in to the SSH tunnels that have no username of their "
"own. A connection that fills in its own username and password uses those "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:536
msgid ""
"An SSH server whose host key isn't in the app's list or in ~/.ssh/"
"known_hosts is normally shown with its fingerprint for you to trust. Turn "
"this on to trust and remember it without asking; a key that changes is "
"always refused."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:537
msgid ""
"A connection that has one of these profiles tints the app's background while "
"you are connected to it, to tell environments apart."
msgstr ""

